# [[ .Name ]]

[[ if eq .Kind "qmock" -]]
A qmock: a stand-in quanar for developing quans. It is the quanar template itself; its
database is kept in memory, so a quan can be tried without the real quanar or a real database.
[[- else -]]
A quanar: one server process. It holds no business logic. It loads quans at runtime,
listens to what they ask it to listen to and does the work they ask for through the qua.
[[- end ]]
[[ if not .Quas ]]
> **No qua yet.** Add a qua to `package.json`, import it in `src/quan-host`, give it a core
> there and in `src/core/qua-core`, and list it in a quan's `quas` in `src/config/quan-sources`.
[[ end ]]
## How a quan arrives

1. `src/config/quan-sources` lists each quan: where its file is, its event stream and the quas plugged into it.
2. The quanar subscribes to the event stream. When it opens, the file is downloaded and, if the list
   gives a `hash`, checked; a file that does not match never runs.
3. The quan runs in its own Node process (`src/quan-host`), with the permission model on, an empty
   environment and a memory limit. It only gets the quas plugged into it.
4. `api.get('/notes', …)` in the quan makes the quanar listen to `GET /notes`; requests are handed to the
   quan's process. `db.create('notes', …)` comes back to the quanar's `db-manager`.
5. A `change` event reloads the quan; when the stream closes the quan is unmounted at once.

## Layout

- `src/core`: `api-manager` (who listens to what), `db-manager` (in memory; replace it to use a real
  database), `http-server`, `quan-loader`, `quan-process`, `event-stream`, `qua-core`, `logger`
- `src/quan-host`: the program each quan's process runs; quanar code, built to `dist/quan-host.cjs`
- `src/services`: `quan-service` (follows the quans), `system-service` (`GET /health`, `GET /quans`)

Lines marked `// qu:` are where `qu` adds quans and quas. Do not delete them; you may move them.

```sh
npm run dev      # builds and starts on port [[ if eq .Kind "qmock" ]]3001[[ else ]]3000[[ end ]]
```

| Variable | Default | |
|---|---|---|
| `PORT` | [[ if eq .Kind "qmock" ]]3001[[ else ]]3000[[ end ]] | |
| `RECONNECT_MS` | 2000 | wait before knocking on a closed quan again |
| `REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS` | 10000 | a quan that does not answer in time is stopped |
